course: dictionary
lesson: 3860
title: Short words with many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An abbreviation is a short form of a longer word or name. «Fr» is an abbreviation, but it is also a fragment, a piece that has no meaning on its own. It can stand for different things, so you must read the context to know which one it means.
explain: In «Fr. Michael led the service this morning», the dot and the name in front of the word tell you it is a title. In church, «Fr» is short for Father, the name for a priest. The clue is the name that follows it, not the letters alone.
explain: In a chat, «that's funny fr» is a different story. Nobody is talking about a priest or a language there. The word «funny» and the casual tone show that «fr» means «for real», so the friend is saying they really mean it.
fact: Fr is short for Father, the title of a priest, as in «Fr. Michael».
fact: Fr can be short for French or France, and fr is the code for French on computers and language menus. Web addresses ending «.fr» belong to France.
fact: In texting, «fr» means «for real», as in «that's funny fr».
fact: Fr is also the chemical symbol for francium, a rare element on the periodic table.
fact: Fr was short for franc, old French money. Swiss francs are still used today.
exercise: «Fr. Michael led the service this morning.» What does Fr mean here? | Francium | French | For real | *Father
exercise: «That's funny fr.» What does fr mean in this message? | French | Francium | *For real | Franc
exercise: A web address ends with «.fr». What does fr tell you? | *French | For real | Father | Francium
test: «She sent hearts every day and said ur my bestie fr.» What does fr mean here? | Francium | *For real | French | Father
test: Which meaning of Fr is a chemical symbol on the periodic table? | Father | Franc | *Francium | French
exam: Why do you need the context to understand «Fr»? | It is always the same in every text | It has no meaning at all | *It can mean different things, such as Father, French, for real or francium | It is only ever used for money
